{"content":[{"c":["SHESHAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Descendant of Judah through Jerahmeel, whose family line is traced in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.25-41","r":"1Chr.2.25-41","rawR":"1Chr.2.25-41","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.25-41","value":"1Chr.2.25-41"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 2:25-41"}," to Elishama, evidently a contemporary of the writer. In verse ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.31","r":"1Chr.2.31","rawR":"1Chr.2.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.31","value":"1Chr.2.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"31"}," Sheshan’s son Ahlai is named, but verse ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.34","r":"1Chr.2.34","rawR":"1Chr.2.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.34","value":"1Chr.2.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"34"}," says that Sheshan had no sons. Perhaps two men of the same name are denoted here, or Ahlai may be identical with Attai, Sheshan’s grandson."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Sheshan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 2:25-41","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.25-41","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.25-41","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.25-41"},{"anchorText":"31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.31","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.31","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.31"},{"anchorText":"34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.34","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.34","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.34"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0864abd2f590ded52b9a7063292a44a46220dd08bfc2a0b743bf9d56c93c722c","sourceItemName":"Sheshan","sourceItemOrder":301,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Sheshan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Sheshan","title":"Sheshan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}